<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II, Duke of Brunswick</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1873</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, succeeded his father, who was killed at Quatre Bras in 1815, and took power in 1823. His arbitrary rule provoked a rising in September 1830 that burned his palace and drove him out. The German Confederation recognised his brother William as duke, and Charles lived the rest of his life in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-duke-of-brunswick.jpg" alt="Charles II, Duke of Brunswick" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknow artist · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CarlBraunsweichWelf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
